 "chips_saved_L": 6.0,
 "method": "Deflection: an end mill as a cantilever, delta = F L^3 / (3 E I), with I = pi D_e^4 / 64 and D_e = 0.8 D (Mitsubishi Materials models an end mill as a solid rod of 0.7-0.8 D; 0.7 D bends 1.7x more), E = 600 GPa (WC-Co), per 100 N of radial load, which is about what a full-height finishing pass in 6061 puts on a 3/4 in. tool (0.25 mm radial, 0.05 mm/tooth, ~60 mm of flute engaged, K_c ~ 700 N/mm2: ~240 N tangential, ~0.4 of that radial). The holder and spindle add to it; this is the tool alone. Volumes come from cam_sim.json (voxel stock-removal runs) where it has them."
